WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is a writer,
director, and producer

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from his work
on "Trainwreck,"

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Knocked Up," and
"The 40-Year-Old Virgin,"

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as "Girls"
and "Freaks and Geeks."

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
His new film,
"The King of Staten Island,"

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.843 line:92%
is available on demand now

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:13.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's my conversation wit
our friend Judd Apatow.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:16.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
Judd, it's great to see you.
How are you doing?

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm doing well.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been home
for over three months.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.655 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And this is the result.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's lovely.
It's beautiful.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you're in bloom.
You're in full bloom.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.796 size:84% position:42%
-Do you know that I did
my own makeup today?

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.598 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-No. Get out of here.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.599 line:92%
-This is -- you know what,

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always have these
makeup people.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can do it myself, which is
basically Irish Spring.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I use Irish Spring.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then this is it.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.610 line:92%
I don't even have beard oil in

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.911 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-How do the women --

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
the three women
that you live with feel

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.947 line:92%
about your look right now?

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.984
-They feel the same way yo
feel, that it looks great.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That I'm glad
that we found this.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot of support.
A lot of support.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.256
-No, they are so annoyed because
they think it's too big

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:59.592
and they're mad I won't trim it,
but I'm going kind of

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a Benjamin Harrison look
-Yes.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they're mad at me because
I keep saying,

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, then I'm going to
shave it all off."

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like, "No, we don'
want to see your face!"

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they want
a little beard,

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.740 size:81% position:41% line:92%
but they hate my face.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I try to remind them,
"It's your face."

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right.
-Like my face looks

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.211 size:84% position:42% line:92%
kind of like your face.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't hate it that much.
-No, of course not.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's very fair.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
Although, it's not really
their fault,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.652 line:92%
but it's a fair assessment

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.220 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So, the movie's great.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.890
And I want to talk, becaus
I feel like you always do

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
such an incredible job
with casting,

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially casting that people
wouldn't expect.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, obviously Marisa Tomei
is so great in this movie.

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Steve Buscemi.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, Pete is so much fu
to watch.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bill Burr is fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
But maybe Action Bronson
steals the movie.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-People aren't really
talking yet enough about

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:53.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Action Bronson
has a key role in the movie.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:56.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we needed a strang
neighborhood figure.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to give away what
happens in the sequence.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:03.423
And Action Bronson was the onl
one who was hysterically funny

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.424 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And also Machine --

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.960 size:75% position:38%
Machine Gun Kelly is
in the movie as well

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.062 line:92%
as a mean tattoo shop owner.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:12.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know,
I love having cameos like,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
RZA is in "Funny People."
-Yeah.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.303 size:78% position:39%
-And Ghostface Killah
is in "Walk Hard."

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Method Man
is in "Trainwreck."

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:21.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm just working throug
the whole Wu-Tang Clan.

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:22.075 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's my tribute to
Staten Island over a career.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:26.779 size:84% position:42%
-That's very -- that's
very nice of you to do.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had Pete on and he talked
about, you know,

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
writing a first draft
of this movie.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
I imagine, like,
for somebody like him

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.421 size:84% position:42%
who's playing the lead
in a film that is also,

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.358
you know, to some degree
pulled from his own life,

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:43.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
did he have anxiety
in the early days of shooting?

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.898 line:92%
-You know, he got very nervous

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:46.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
right before
we started shooting.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:50.703
So, you know, we were having fun
writing for a couple of years.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the night before
shooting started,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just started getting these
e-mails from him.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:59.646
And he was sending me the IMDB
resumes of actors he thought

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.214 line:92%
should be better than him.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like,
"Can I not go to work tomorrow

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.585 size:88% position:44% line:92%
What about Emile Hirsch?

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, what about
Cole Sprouse?"

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
And all these resumes
keep popping up.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:12.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm at home laughing
thinking, oh, he's hysterical.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.026 line:92%
This Pete, he's hysterical

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the next day at wor
he's like, "I'm serious.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
You should have called
Cole Sprouse."

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-"I really --

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really don't want to be here
today, Judd."

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then after the first day
he got really comfortable

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.371 line:92%
and had a blast making it.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:28.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he certainly was a littl
nervous heading into it.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:32.145
-A directors fear, one of thei
many fears on set is something

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:35.715
will change with an actor an
there will be continuity issues.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was your biggest
continuity fear about Pete

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:43.823
-The biggest fear I had wa
he loves getting tattoos.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.390 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's just like
the after like,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.260 line:92%
"Oh, look how good it looks.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's the process
of getting it.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
He talked a lot about enjoying
the fact that it hurt

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:57.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that it focused him
and helped him think clearly

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.273
And we talked a lot about trying
to understand that.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.775 size:88% position:44%
And so, he kept asking
if he could get a tattoo

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a weird place that
wouldn't be in the movie.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "I don't kno
when I need you naked.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:09.849
I might need you naked one day
You can't have a new tattoo.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I was worried
he would go

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
like full Post Malone
at some point.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, sure.
-Because that would happen -

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:18.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we were doing "Girls,
in between seasons,

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
they would get tattoos
and they wouldn't ask anybody.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
They would just show up and go
"Do you love these tattoos

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:25.732 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I got all over my hands?

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:28.935
And I'm like, "I guess you
character just got tattoos

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:31.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
on her hands."
-Man, yeah.

